[2026-01-30T12:25:25.261Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Consolidate visualization theme system to eliminate repetitive color patterns across 8+ components\n\n## Context Area\nData Visualizations\n\n## Description\nConsolidate visualization theme system to eliminate repetitive color patterns across 8+ components\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\nExtract shared visualization theme logic into a centralized theme configuration system that eliminates repetitive `isRadar ? 'radar-color' : 'swiss-color'` patterns across 15+ components. This will reduce code duplication, ensure visual consistency, and make theme extensions (adding new themes) trivial.\n\n## Business Value\n- Reduces code duplication by ~40% across visualization components\n- Makes adding new themes a single-file change instead of touching 15+ files\n- Eliminates subtle visual inconsistencies between components\n- Improves developer experience when building new visualizations\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Create unified theme configuration with semantic color tokens\n- Refactor existing visualization components to use theme tokens\n- Create theme-aware utility components for common patterns\n\n**Excluded:**\n- Video playback system (already well-abstracted)\n- Report core components (separate concern)\n\n## Key Components\n1. `ThemeTokens` configuration - defines semantic colors per theme\n2. `useVisualizationTheme` hook - provides theme-aware color getters\n3. Theme-aware styled primitives for common SVG/div patterns\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Audit all visualization files for repeated color patterns\n2. Create semantic token system (primary, secondary, accent, muted, etc.)\n3. Build useVisualizationTheme hook with type-safe color accessors\n4. Refactor components one-by-one to use new system\n5. Add validation to ensure all tokens are defined per theme\n\n## Files to Modify\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/Timeline.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/CausalFlow.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/TrustRadar.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/ConfidenceHeatmap.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/ContradictionMatrix.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/NetworkGraph.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/SourceNetwork.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/EntityConstellation.tsx` - replace inline colors\n- Create new: `src/components/report/visualizations/theme.ts`\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] No inline `isRadar ? x : y` color patterns in visualization components\n- [ ] All visualizations use semantic theme tokens\n- [ ] Adding a new theme requires only theme.ts changes\n- [ ] TypeScript enforces all tokens are defined per theme\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Ensuring all edge cases are covered by semantic tokens - mitigate with comprehensive audit first\n- Migration may temporarily break visual consistency - mitigate with component-by-component refactor\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cec20cb-b613-4ab4-b437-0d4075a2df3d","uuid":"f7158a32-0ddc-4306-b519-602e996ad084","isSynthetic":true}
